  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q9",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x^2$. Determine whether the following statements are true or false.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(4x)=16f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(4x)&=(4x)^2\\\\f(4x)&=16x^2\\\\f(4x)&=16f(x)\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(xy)=f(x)\\times f(y)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(xy)&=(xy)^2\\\\f(xy)&=x^2y^2\\\\f(xy)&=f(x)\\times f(y)\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)=\\frac{f(x)}{f(y)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "For $y\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)&=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)^2\\\\f\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)&=\\frac{x^2}{y^2}\\\\f\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)&=\\frac{f(x)}{f(y)}\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x^2)=(f(x))^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x^2)&=(x^2)^2\\\\f(x^2)&=(f(x))^2\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x+y)=f(x)+f(y)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x+y)&=(x+y)^2\\\\f(x+y)&=x^2+2xy+y^2\\end{align*}$$\nThe right-hand side is $x^2+y^2$. For example, $x=y=1$ gives $f(2)=4$ and $f(1)+f(1)=2$. False.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(\\sqrt{x+y})=f(\\sqrt{x})+f(\\sqrt{y})$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $x,y\\ge0$.",
          "worked": "For $x,y\\ge0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(\\sqrt{x+y})&=(\\sqrt{x+y})^2\\\\f(\\sqrt{x+y})&=x+y\\end{align*}$$\nAlso,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(\\sqrt{x})+f(\\sqrt{y})&=(\\sqrt{x})^2+(\\sqrt{y})^2\\\\f(\\sqrt{x})+f(\\sqrt{y})&=x+y\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$f(x+y)+f(x-y)=2[f(x)+f(y)]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x+y)+f(x-y)&=(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2\\\\f(x+y)+f(x-y)&=x^2+2xy+y^2+x^2-2xy+y^2\\\\f(x+y)+f(x-y)&=2x^2+2y^2\\\\f(x+y)+f(x-y)&=2[f(x)+f(y)]\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$f\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)=2+f(x)+f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)&=\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)^2\\\\f\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)&=x^2+2+\\frac1{x^2}\\\\f\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)&=2+f(x)+f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nTrue.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      }
    ]
  },
